{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"SEQUENCING CONSTRAINT INVERTED — my own 'land nothing until cc33 merges' was wrong, and CI proved it.\n\nThe full suite on the integrated stack fails ONE test:\n\n  tests/unit/test_structured_run_seam.py::test_runner_regains_real_headroom_under_the_cap\n  AssertionError: runner.py is 782 LOC; the split must bring it under 700\n\nThat is task 3a98's headroom guard, whose docstring reads 'runner.py must stop sitting ON the 800\ngate, not merely pass it'. It is doing exactly its job: cc33's +97 lines regrew the file past the\nheadroom a previous split bought. 8221 passed, 1 failed.\n\nTHE CIRCULARITY: this parent said land nothing here until cc33 merges, because cc33 touches regions\nthese children move. But cc33 cannot merge while it breaks this work's own precondition.\n\nRESOLVED, and the constraint is narrower than I wrote it: the real requirement was never 'wait for\ncc33 to merge', it was 'do not AUTHOR against a pre-cc33 base', because the diff would be wrong.\ncc33 is now cherry-picked INTO the working stack (a3c4fd472), so extracting on top of it satisfies\nthe intent exactly and there is no rebase conflict — the extraction moves the POST-cc33 code.\n\nSo the children land WITH cc33 in the same stack, not after it merges. Updating the constraint here\nrather than leaving a note that would send the next reader in a circle.\n\nARITHMETIC, so nobody expects one extraction to be enough:\n  782 - 75  (e6bd, the except spine)          = 707   STILL OVER the 700 guard\n  707 - 80  (8229, the settings block)        = ~627  under\na49e (the session guard) is roughly LOC-neutral — it swaps a construct+finally for a .\nSo BOTH extractions are required before this stack can be pushed green, not just the first.\n\nNOT relaxing the guard. Lowering a threshold that exists to catch precisely this is the 'raise the\ncap' anti-pattern ADR 0056 rejects by name, and it would discard the one mechanism that caught the\nregression."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785513985742272001,"uuid":"6336097f-0c95-4f73-951b-5012f3643e50"}